msgid "**Syntax**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:46
msgid ""
"Select the attribute denoted by attribute path _attrpath_ from [attribute "
"set](./types.md#type-attrs) _attrset_. If the attribute doesn’t exist, "
"return the _expr_ after `or` if provided, otherwise abort evaluation."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:51
msgid "Function application"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:57
msgid ""
"Apply the callable value _func_ to the argument _expr_. Note the absence of "
"any visible operator symbol. A callable value is either:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:59
msgid "a [user-defined function](./syntax.md#functions)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:60
msgid "a [built-in](./builtins.md) function"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:61
msgid ""
"an attribute set with a [`__functor` attribute](./syntax.md#attr-__functor)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:63 source/language/operators.md:301
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:65
msgid ""
"[List](./types.md#type-list) items are also separated by whitespace, which "
"means that function calls in list items must be enclosed by parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:67
msgid "Has attribute"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:73
msgid ""
"Test whether _expr_ is an [attribute set](./types.md#type-attrs) containing "
"the attribute denoted by _[attrpath](./syntax.md#attrpath-literal)_. If "
"_attrpath_ contains multiple components, and any of its components (other "
"than the last) do not correspond to an attribute set in _expr_, the result "
"is false. The result is a [Boolean](./types.md#type-bool) value."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:77
msgid ""
"See also: [`builtins.hasAttr`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-hasAttr)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:85
msgid ""
"After evaluating _attrset_ and _attrpath_, the computational complexity is "
"O(log(_n_)) for _n_ attributes in the _attrset_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:87
msgid "Arithmetic"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:89
msgid ""
"Numbers will retain their type unless mixed with other numeric types: Pure "
"integer operations will always return integers, whereas any operation "
"involving at least one floating point number returns a floating point number."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:92
msgid ""
"Evaluation of the following numeric operations throws an evaluation error:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:93
msgid "Division by zero"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:94
msgid ""
"Integer overflow, that is, any operation yielding a result outside of the "
"representable range of [Nix language integers](./syntax.md#number-literal)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:96
msgid "See also [Comparison](#comparison) and [Equality](#equality)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:98
msgid "The `+` operator is overloaded to also work on strings and paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:102
msgid "String concatenation"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:108
msgid ""
"Concatenate two [strings](./types.md#type-string) and merge their [string "
"contexts](./string-context.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:112
msgid "Path concatenation"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:118
msgid "Concatenate two [paths](./types.md#type-path). The result is a path."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:123
msgid "Path and string concatenation"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:127
msgid "_path_ + _string_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:129
msgid ""
"Concatenate _[path](./types.md#type-path)_ with _[string](./types.md#type-"
"string)_. The result is a path."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:132
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:134
msgid ""
"The string must not have a [string context](./string-context.md) that refers "
"to a [store path](../store/store-path.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:138
msgid "String and path concatenation"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:142
msgid "_string_ + _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:144
msgid ""
"Concatenate _[string](./types.md#type-string)_ with _[path](./types.md#type-"
"path)_. The result is a string."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:147
msgid "**Important**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:149
msgid ""
"The file or directory at _path_ must exist and is copied to the [store](../"
"glossary.md#gloss-store). The path appears in the result as the "
"corresponding [store path](../store/store-path.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:157
msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:161
msgid "_attrset1_ // _attrset2_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:163
msgid ""
"Update [attribute set](./types.md#type-attrs) _attrset1_ with names and "
"values from _attrset2_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:165
msgid ""
"The returned attribute set will have all of the attributes in _attrset1_ and "
"_attrset2_. If an attribute name is present in both, the attribute value "
"from the latter is taken."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:168
msgid ""
"This operator is [strict](../language/evaluation.md#strictness) in both "
"_attrset1_ and _attrset2_. That means that both arguments are evaluated to "
"[weak head normal form](../language/evaluation.md#values), so the attribute "
"sets themselves are evaluated, but their attribute values are not evaluated."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:173
msgid "Comparison"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:175
msgid "Comparison is"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:177
msgid "[arithmetic](#arithmetic) for [numbers](./types.md#type-float)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:178
msgid ""
"lexicographic for [strings](./types.md#type-string) and [paths](./types."
"md#type-path)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:179
msgid ""
"item-wise lexicographic for [lists](./types.md#type-list): elements at the "
"same index in both lists are compared according to their type and skipped if "
"they are equal."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:182
msgid ""
"All comparison operators are implemented in terms of `<`, and the following "
"equivalencies hold:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:184
msgid "comparison"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:184
msgid "implementation"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:186
msgid "_a_ `<=` _b_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:186
msgid "`! (` _b_ `<` _a_ `)`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:187
msgid "_a_ `>`  _b_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:187
msgid "_b_ `<` _a_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:188
msgid "_a_ `>=` _b_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:188
msgid "`! (` _a_ `<` _b_ `)`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:192
msgid "Equality"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:194
msgid ""
"[Attribute sets](./types.md#type-attrs) are compared first by attribute "
"names and then by items until a difference is found."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:195
msgid ""
"[Lists](./types.md#type-list) are compared first by length and then by items "
"until a difference is found."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:196
msgid ""
"Comparison of distinct [functions](./syntax.md#functions) returns `false`, "
"but identical functions may be subject to [value identity optimization]"
"(#value-identity-optimization)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:197
msgid "Numbers are type-compatible, see [arithmetic](#arithmetic) operators."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:198
msgid "Floating point numbers only differ up to a limited precision."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:200
msgid ""
"The `==` operator is [strict](../language/evaluation.md#strictness) in both "
"arguments; when comparing composite types ([attribute sets](./types.md#type-"
"attrs) and [lists](./types.md#type-list)), it is partially strict in their "
"contained values: they are evaluated until a difference is found. <!-- this "
"is woefully underspecified, affecting which expressions evaluate correctly; "
"not just \"ordering\" or error messages. -->"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:202
msgid "Value identity optimization"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:204
msgid ""
"Nix performs equality comparisons of nested values by pointer equality or "
"more abstractly, _identity_. Nix semantics ideally do not assign a unique "
"identity to values as they are created, but equality is an exception to this "
"rule. The disputable benefit of this is that it is more efficient, and it "
"allows cyclical structures to be compared, e.g. `let x = { x = x; }; in x == "
"x` evaluates to `true`. However, as a consequence, it makes a function equal "
"to itself when the comparison is made in a list or attribute set, in "
"contradiction to a simple direct comparison."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:213
msgid "Logical conjunction"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:217
msgid "_bool1_ `&&` _bool2_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:219
msgid "Logical AND. Equivalent to `if` _bool1_ `then` _bool2_ `else false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:221 source/language/operators.md:272
msgid ""
"This operator is [strict](../language/evaluation.md#strictness) in _bool1_, "
"but only evaluates _bool2_ if _bool1_ is `true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:223 source/language/operators.md:245
#: source/language/operators.md:274 source/language/operators.md:291
msgid "**Example**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:225
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"true && false\n"
"=> false\n"
"\n"
"false && throw \"never evaluated\"\n"
"=> false\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:235
msgid "Logical disjunction"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:239
msgid "_bool1_ `||` _bool2_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:241
msgid "Logical OR. Equivalent to `if` _bool1_ `then true` `else` _bool2_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:243
msgid ""
"This operator is [strict](../language/evaluation.md#strictness) in _bool1_, "
"but only evaluates _bool2_ if _bool1_ is `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:247
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"true || false\n"
"=> true\n"
"\n"
"true || throw \"never evaluated\"\n"
"=> true\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:257
msgid "Precedence and disjunctive normal form"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:259
msgid ""
"The precedence of `&&` and `||` aligns with disjunctive normal form. Without "
"parentheses, an expression describes multiple \"permissible "
"situations\" (connected by `||`), where each situation consists of multiple "
"simultaneous conditions (connected by `&&`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:262
msgid ""
"For example, `A || B && C || D && E` is parsed as `A || (B && C) || (D && "
"E)`, describing three permissible situations: A holds, or both B and C hold, "
"or both D and E hold."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:264
msgid "Logical implication"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:268
msgid "_bool1_ `->` _bool2_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:270
msgid ""
"Logical implication. Equivalent to `!`_bool1_ `||` _bool2_ (or `if` _bool1_ "
"`then` _bool2_ `else true`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:276
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"true -> false\n"
"=> false\n"
"\n"
"false -> throw \"never evaluated\"\n"
"=> true\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:286
msgid "Pipe operators"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:288
msgid "_a_ `|>` _b_ is equivalent to _b_ _a_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/operators.md:289
msgid "_a_ `<|` _b_ is equivalent to _a_ _b_"
msgstr ""

